  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Human Rights Due Diligence and Decent Work in the Sugarcane Sector through the Use of New Technology and Multi-Stakeholder Engagement</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project partners will apply global expertise in migrant-centred and gender sensitive participatory and community-based engagement models, including Participatory Rural Appraisal (PRA) methods and tools as well as robust and field-tested migrant-centred HRDD methodologies (led by IOM). These will be adjusted to a context of conducting digital HRDD (led by Diginex) in complex global agricultural supply chains (of Unilever and Coca-Cola). By doing so, this intervention will aim to develop and test a new scalable and innovative model for engagement of suppliers including small holder farmers (direct employers), as well as men and women migrant workers in the sugarcane sector, that can be applied to other vulnerable populations employed in agricultural sectors</narrative>
  </description>
